## Project State Summary

**Problem:** go-unix-utils is a specification-driven experiment that regenerates Unix utilities in Go from C-source-derived specs, verified via differential testing against GNU reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation pipeline.

**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Human writes PRDs and use cases; orchestrator generates Go code in `cmd/` and `pkg/`; differential testing harness (`pkg/testutils`) validates output parity against Homebrew GNU binaries.

**Current state:** 17 commands implemented across generation runs (tee, head, seq, echo, tac, nl, fold, expand, unexpand, cut, paste, uniq, comm, md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum), plus foundation packages (pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format) and earlier utilities (ts, cat, wc, sponge) at generation-merged tags. All releases through rel05.4 are marked "implemented." Code lives at generation tags, not on the working branch.

**Target release:** rel99.2 — the only release in scope. Contains one use case: `rel99.2-uc001-ts` (ts utility, spec_complete, code not started on working branch).

## Priority Reasoning

Release 99.2 has a single use case: `ts` from moreutils. The specs (PRD, use case, test suite) are complete. The code existed at earlier generation tags but needs regeneration on the current branch. Per the split rule (implementation before tests, max 1 task), I propose the implementation task.

```yaml
- index: 0
  title: "rel99.2-uc001-ts: cmd/ts implementation"
  dependency: -1
  description: |
    deliverable_type: code

    required_reading:
      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (find the ts PRD -- likely prd004-ts.yaml or prd005-ts.yaml)
      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel99.2-uc001-ts.yaml (ts use case with success criteria)
      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-99.2.yaml (ts test suite with expected inputs/outputs)
      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared_protocols section -- SIGPIPE handling and differential testing pattern)
      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests, BuildBinary API)
      - pkg/sys/signal.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler function)

    files:
      - path: cmd/ts/main.go
        action: create
        note: ts utility -- reads stdin lines, prepends timestamps, writes to stdout
      - path: cmd/ts/ts_test.go
        action: create
        note: differential tests against moreutils ts reference binary

    requirements:
      - id: R1
        text: "Implement cmd/ts/main.go per the ts PRD: read lines from stdin, prepend a timestamp to each line, write to stdout. Default format is the PRD-specified strftime format string."
      - id: R2
        text: "Support all flags defined in the ts PRD -- at minimum: optional format string argument, -i (incremental/elapsed since last line), -s (elapsed since program start), and -m (monotonic clock). Derive exact flag set from the PRD."
      - id: R3
        text: "Call pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main() per the project shared protocol for all cmd/ utilities."
      - id: R4
        text: "Implement differential tests in ts_test.go using pkg/testutils.BuildBinary and pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests. Reference binary is \"ts\" from moreutils (Homebrew). Skip gracefully if not in PATH via exec.LookPath."

    design_decisions:
      - id: D1
        text: "Reference binary for differential testing is \"ts\" from moreutils (not g-prefixed -- moreutils does not use the g prefix). Use exec.LookPath(\"ts\") and t.Skip if not found."
      - id: D2
        text: "Follow the differential testing shared protocol from ARCHITECTURE.yaml: BuildBinary(t, \".\"), LookPath for reference, define []testutils.DiffTest, call RunDiffTests."
      - id: D3
        text: "Set LC_ALL=C in test environment per project convention. For timestamp-dependent tests, use testutils.TimestampNormalizer or a custom NormalizeFunc to handle timing differences between Go and reference binary."
      - id: D4
        text: "Do NOT install any packages in the test. If the reference binary is missing, t.Skip. This is a hard project rule."

    acceptance_criteria:
      - id: AC1
        text: "cmd/ts/main.go compiles without errors via go build ./cmd/ts/"
      - id: AC2
        text: "go vet ./cmd/ts/ reports no issues"
      - id: AC3
        text: "cmd/ts/ts_test.go contains differential tests covering the flags and behaviors specified in the ts PRD"
      - id: AC4
        text: "All differential tests pass when the moreutils ts binary is in PATH"
      - id: AC5
        text: "Tests skip gracefully with t.Skip when ts is not in PATH"
      - id: AC6
        text: "main() calls sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() before any I/O"
```